From f17f9a66d57b80df9bdaf821cb61fe47a2cc9090 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:31:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rawdanger-recomp: v0.8.2 ambient occlusion from the game's
 depth

- gs.wgsl game_ao: before Raw Danger's colour filter (at the walk's start, so the filter tints the shading as the game's own
  light), creases are found from pairs of depth samples on opposite sides of each pixel (the game's depth is about 1 / distance,
  linear across a flat surface: floors and walls stay clear), sized by depth, with a range check against objects far in front
- ps2::set_ambient_occlusion (0 off, 1 light, 2 strong); keys.ini ambient_occlusion, F1 > Picture

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
